<details><summary>Reveal why separations also transfer</summary>
Suppose a language appears at level $n+1$ but not at level $n$. Forward transport preserves upper-level membership. If it appeared at the lower level on the destination, backward transport would put it at the lower source level, a contradiction.
</details>

## Witnesses and the P-versus-NP form

A witness verifier accepts pairs $(x,w)$ and recognizes $x$ when some certificate $w$ is accepted. Exact verifier translations preserve the same witnesses and costs. Therefore the equality—or inequality—between deterministic and witness classes cannot be changed by an exact substrate replacement.

For background, see the [P versus NP overview](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/P_versus_NP_problem) and [many-one reduction](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Many-one_reduction). These links provide context; all results used here are stated in the accompanying paper.

## Stronger computation and the next horizon

A jump hierarchy places $J^n(S)$ at tier $n$ while keeping $J^{n+1}(S)$ outside that tier. Move the slider and watch the horizon recede.

